\subsection*{Fundamental Theorem of Arithmetic}

Every integer $n > 1$ can be expressed as a product of prime numbers. This representation is unique, except for the order of factors.

\textcolor{primaryblue}{\faInfoCircle\ \textbf{In other words:}}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Existence:} Every integer greater than 1 can be factored into primes
    \item \textbf{Uniqueness:} This factorization is unique (up to reordering)
\end{itemize}

