\textcolor{primaryblue}{\faLightbulb\ \textbf{Practical Application}}

This theorem gives us an efficient method to test if a number is prime:

\textbf{To check if $n$ is prime:}
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Calculate $\sqrt{n}$
    \item Test divisibility by all primes $p \leq \sqrt{n}$
    \item If none divide $n$, then $n$ is prime
    \item If any divides $n$, then $n$ is composite
\end{enumerate}

This significantly reduces the number of divisibility tests needed!

